@@ -1,5 +1,23 @@
 {#-
-  This file was automatically generated - do not edit
+  Renders the docs site's left pane with the same rows as the landing page's pane.
+
+  This is Material's own partials/nav.html with two rows added around the stock loop.
+  Home links back to the landing page and opens to its sections. External resources
+  lists the project's outside links. Both read config.extra.acs_nav in mkdocs.yml, the
+  one source the landing renderer reads too, so the two panes cannot drift apart.
+
+  The two rows match the byte contract in tests/test_site_nav_walk.py, which the pane
+  walkers and the pane comparison read. External resources is a section, always open,
+  so its toggle stays unchecked. Home is never the current page on a docs page, so it
+  never carries aria-current.
+
+  The landing root is this page's base_url plus "/..". On 404.html base_url is a
+  rooted path that may end in a slash, which the replace folds. The theme environment
+  has autoescape off, so every emitted value carries the e filter. The template uses
+  filters only, never a Python method call, so it also renders under MiniJinja.
+
+  The installed partial and the diff to this file live in overrides/.upstream/partials.
+  After editing this file, run: uv run python tools/rederive_overrides.py --record
 -#}
 {% import "partials/nav-item.html" as item with context %}
 {% set class = "md-nav md-nav--primary" %}
